  90: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  91:     """
  92:     Extend the diagonal blue ray through the grid, reflecting it off red line-segment mirrors.
  93: 
  94:     Input structure
  95:     - Black-background grid with one diagonal 8-connected blue ray seed.
  96:     - Red foreground objects, when present, are straight horizontal or vertical mirror segments.
  97:     - Other foreground bars are transparent to the ray and may be overwritten where the ray crosses them.
  98: 
  99:     Rule
 100:     - Start from the ray seed endpoint whose outward diagonal extension remains inside the grid.
 101:     - Paint the ray continuously in that diagonal direction until it leaves the grid.
 102:     - If the next cell is a red mirror, do not paint it; reflect by flipping the row direction on a horizontal mirror or the column direction on a vertical mirror.
 103: 
 104:     Key insight
 105:     - The non-red bars are decoys: only red bars reflect the diagonal path, while all other crossed cells become blue.
 106:     """
