  14:     Copy the four corner patterns into a minimal square output frame.
  15: 
  16:     Input structure:
  17:     - Same-color patterns occupy square regions in the four input corners.
  18:     - Black cells separate the corner regions.
  19:     - At least one foreground pixel is present.
  20: 
  21:     Rule:
  22:     - Assign foreground pixels to their nearest input corner.
  23:     - Infer the largest needed corner square side length.
  24:     - Copy each corner square into the corresponding corner of an output one cell larger.
  25: 
  26:     Key insight:
  27:     - The task preserves each pattern's corner-relative offsets while shrinking the canvas.
  28:     """
